request:
{
 "project": "Gemini Software Requirements Specification",
 "meeting": "1 of 1 (kickoff)",
 "participants": [
  "Analyst",
  "Client",
  "EndUser",
  "TechLead"
 ],
 "previous_turns_for_context_only": [
  {
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "In the event that the risk persists, subsystems must be able to move themselves into safe states to protect people and equipment (i.e. if there is a failure in the higher-level systems)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "content": [
    "Safety protection must be applied whenever there is the risk that the actions of the control software could endanger people or cause damage to any Gemini 8m Telescopes subsystem, for example, by driving beyond limits or by overexposing detectors."
   ]
  }
 ],
 "turns": [
  {
   "id": "M1:T101",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "In general this will require mechanical hard stops, electrical interlocks, electrical hard limit switches, soft limit switches, software limits, and watch dogs,.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T102",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Safety aspects shall be analyzed during the functional specification phase of the software.",
     "role": "statement"
    },
    {
     "text": "Security must be provided in order to both prevent accidental mix-up of commands from different users on different parts of the system and to prevent intrusion from the wide area network into the Gemini 8m Telescopes.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T103",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T104",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "In particular, the astronomical database must be protected from intrusion, whether the purpose is to access private data or to be destructive.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T105",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'testabilty' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T106",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "This plan will address all areas of testing from design, acceptance, commissioning through to hand-over.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T107",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'modularity' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T108",
   "speaker": "TechLead",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "At the same time, the possibility must exist to acquire information about other parts of the system (for example, telescope coordinates) (as mentioned in the control flow requirements in Section 3.1.1).",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T109",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'installation aspects' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T110",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Every system must thus be able to supply its current version upon request.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T111",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'remote operations' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T112",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "There must be some form of security to control access to system features, possibly restricting some operations to specific remote sites (e.g. Hale Pohaku or Hilo in Hawaii, Cerro Tololo in Chile, etc.)",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T113",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T114",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "anything_else",
   "guide": "Analyst asks whether there is anything else on 'remote operations'."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T115",
   "speaker": "Client",
   "act": "nothing_else",
   "guide": "Short answer: nothing else on this topic."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T116",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'normal operation' and asks about it."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T117",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Start-up and shut-down. There are start-up and shut-down procedures that must exist at many different levels: Cold start-up, starting the system from scratch (including time to download all software) should take about 5 minutes. This does not include time to start-up the telescope or instruments. Warm start-up, starting from scratch but also excluding software download time should take about 1 minute. Telescope start-up, measured from end of cold or warm start-up should be about 4 minutes. Instrument start-up, measured from end of telescope start-up, should take 2 minutes or less.There must be a way to shut down all subsystems (hardware and software). All start-ups and shut-downs are to be automatically logged with time stamps, to allow for statistics on system availability.",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T118",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "backchannel",
   "guide": "Short acknowledgment while listening (1-3 words)."
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T119",
   "speaker": "EndUser",
   "act": "state",
   "guide": "The speaker states the content in their own words.",
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Engineering Logging It must be possible to log engineering data at up to 200 Hz rates for short periods of time. This data must be available to external software packages for analysis. Long-term logging of engineering data must be possible at slower (1 Hz or less) rates, into a common format (baselined as SYBASE).",
     "role": "statement"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "M1:T120",
   "speaker": "Analyst",
   "act": "ask_topic",
   "guide": "Analyst moves the discussion to the topic 'operation in failure mode' and asks about it."
  }
 ]
}
